  "solution": "**Given:**\n\np = frac{√{2}+1}{√{2}-1} and q = frac{√{2}-1}{√{2}+1} \n\n**Concept used:**\n\np = 1 / q\n\n**Calculation:**\n\np =frac{√{2}+1}{√{2}-1} \n\n= (√2 + 1)²\n\n⇒ 3 + 2√2\n\nAgain,\n\n q = frac{√{2}-1}{√{2}+1} \n\n= 3 - 2√2\n\np + q = 3 + 2√2 + 3 - 2√2 = 6\n\npq = (3 + 2√2)(3 - 2√2) = 1\n\nWe know that, p3 + q3 = (p + q)3 - 3pq(p + q)\n\n⇒ p3 + q3 = (6)3 - 3 × 1 × 6 = 216 - 3 × 6 = 216 - 18 = 198\n\nNow, p2/q + q2/p = (p3 + q3)/pq = 198/1 = 198\n\n**∴ The correct option is 3**\n\n14c:Tf8d,\n<",
